## DEDUCTIONS (Maximum total: 20 points)
Subtract points for red flags:
- -3 to -5 points for claiming "systems" or "low-level" experience but resume shows only web frameworks (React, Django, Express, Node.js)
- -3 to -5 points for exaggerated performance claims without ANY metrics, profiling tools, or measurement methodology ("optimized performance by 10x" with no evidence)
- -2 to -3 points for listing "Linux" as a core systems skill with no evidence of kernel/systems work (just using Ubuntu as a desktop OS)
- -2 to -3 points for projects without any links (GitHub, live demo, or documentation)
- -1 to -2 points for each buzzword-heavy description without technical substance ("leveraged cutting-edge technologies to deliver scalable solutions")
- -2 points for claiming C/C++ expertise but all demonstrable projects are in Python/JavaScript
- -1 to -2 points for projects with generic names and no systems content ("Calculator", "Todo App", "Weather App")

## DOMAIN-SPECIFIC AWARENESS
When evaluating, be aware that this role may target one of these sub-fields. Award extra credit if the candidate shows depth in any:
- **Embedded Systems:** Bare-metal programming, RTOS (FreeRTOS, Zephyr), device drivers, reading hardware datasheets
- **Kernel/Driver Development:** Linux kernel modules, Linux device model, Windows Driver Framework (WDF)
- **Networking:** Deep TCP/IP stack knowledge, packet processing (DPDK, XDP), NIC programming
- **Virtualization/Cloud Infrastructure:** Hypervisors (KVM, Xen), containers (cgroups, namespaces), VMMs
- **Compilers & Runtimes:** LLVM passes, code generation, garbage collectors, JIT compilation
- **Storage Engines:** LSM trees, B-trees, WAL, MVCC, buffer pool management
- **HFT/Trading Systems:** Matching engines, order books, kernel bypass, FPGA acceleration

